{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The two.</b> One to destroy Sodom and one to save Lot — and that is the one who had come to heal Abraham, and the third who came to announce to Sarah; once he had fulfilled his mission he departed." "<b>The angels.</b> And further on He called them men? When the Shechinah was with them He called them men. Another matter: concerning Abraham, whose strength was great and the angels were regulars with him, He called them men like men; and concerning Lot, He called them angels (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>In the evening.</b> Did it take that long for the angels to go from Hebron to Sodom? Rather, they were angels of mercy and were waiting — perhaps Abraham could plead on their behalf." "<b>And Lot sat in the gate of Sodom.</b> ישב is written — that day they appointed him judge over them (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>And Lot saw, etc.</b> From the house of Abraham he had learned to seek out guests."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:24.207709747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}